<request-parameters>
<!--
  D176 provisional, grouped by Year x ICD-10 CHAPTER. Carries the chapter
  view past D76's 2020 edge, alongside the D76 `icd10_chapter` era. Run
  against live WONDER 2026-09.

  Built from mortality_provisional_causes.xml with two edits (the AAR
  knob + O_PR/O_show_totals are carried over unchanged):
    B_2    D176.V4   -> D176.V2-level1   (Group Results By = ICD Chapter)
    O_ucd  D176.V4   -> D176.V2          (Step 6 radio = the ICD-10 code
                                          hierarchy whose level-1 is Chapter)
  Response cells: year, chapter(label, h=depth), Deaths, Population,
  Crude Rate, Age-Adjusted Rate -> same 6-col `coded` contract as the
  icd10 / icd9 / icd8 eras.

  The 2026-09 dump returned 20 chapters for 2021 — one more than D76's 19:
  D176 has a "Codes for special purposes" (U00-U99) chapter, which is
  where COVID-19 (U07.1) lands. Chapter labels carry no code range, so
  they match the CHAPTER_CANON keys in src/api/causesOfDeath.js directly.
  ALWAYS pass --years=2021-<last full year> (yearMax is a 2030 ceiling).
-->
